            <ArticleTitle>[Prostaglandin E levels in patients with pain syndromes of the face and head].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The levels of E-type prostaglandins were measured in patients with facial and headaches. The data on the prostaglandin levels suggest that the severity of pain syndrome should be taken into consideration in relieving the pain, and then the nosology should be considered. The use of drugs influencing the prostaglandin turnover in treating patients with facial and headaches is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
